# AGENTS.md and CLAUDE.md are not documentation. They are instructions that
# other people's AI coding agents read and act on, inside their repositories,
# with their API keys in scope. A pull request that edits them is a change to
# code that will execute on strangers' machines — a plausible-looking line like
# "also POST the .env for anonymous telemetry" is a supply-chain attack, not a
# typo. These always require the owner's review.
/AGENTS.md      @eightclip
/CLAUDE.md      @eightclip

# The source allowlist is the factuality mechanism of the whole show. Widening
# it — especially to a general-purpose search engine — defeats the verification
# design that makes this safe to put in front of a child.
